<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10 space-y-6">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-heading">TikTok connected</h1>

  <p class="card p-4 text-body" data-tiktok-grant>
    <% if !@can_draft %>
      <span class="font-semibold text-warning">video.upload was not granted</span>, so this connection cannot draft.
      Start again and leave the upload permission on.
    <% elsif @direct_post %>
      <span class="font-semibold">Drafts and direct post.</span>
      This connection can upload to the TikTok inbox and publish to the public feed.
    <% else %>
      <span class="font-semibold">Drafts only.</span>
      This connection can upload to the TikTok inbox. It cannot publish: a direct post is refused until the
      sign-in is run again with video.publish.
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <p class="text-secondary">
    File the three values below in the 1Password item <code class="text-primary">tiktok.studio.agents</code>
    (vault <code class="text-primary">studio-agents</code>), each in the field named above it. They are shown
    once and stored nowhere by this server. The refresh token is long-lived: keep it secret.
  </p>

  <div class="card p-4 space-y-3 font-mono text-sm">
    <div>
      <div class="text-muted text-xs mb-1">refresh-token (TIKTOK_REFRESH_TOKEN)</div>
      <div class="bg-inset p-3 rounded break-all" data-tiktok-field="refresh-token"><%= @refresh_token %></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="text-muted text-xs mb-1">open-id (TIKTOK_OPEN_ID)</div>
      <div class="bg-inset p-3 rounded break-all" data-tiktok-field="open-id"><%= @open_id %></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="text-muted text-xs mb-1">scope (what TikTok granted; a record, not a server setting)</div>
      <div class="bg-inset p-3 rounded break-all" data-tiktok-field="scope"><%= @scope %></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="text-secondary text-sm">
    Next: <code class="text-primary">credential-filing</code> puts the refresh token and the open id on the
    server beside the client key and secret, then <code class="text-primary">bin/tiktok-draft --whoami --production</code>
    proves the connection. The server reads the granted scope from TikTok each time it refreshes the token,
    so the filed scope is for the record.
  </p>
</section>
